+// ASSEMBLER_TESTs for the ppc64 (ELFv2, little-endian, POWER8 floor)
+// assembler: gate G2 of work/stubs/M3-BOOT-PLAN.md. Generated code is
+// entered as a plain ELFv2 C function (ppc64 is never simulated): arguments
+// in r3..r10 and f1..f13, result in r3 or f1. Bodies use the volatile
+// registers only (r0, r3-r12, f0-f13, cr0/cr1/cr5-cr7) unless they save the
+// others themselves.
+//
+// The standalone tiers (work/asm/test/tier2, tier3) already prove each
+// macro's encoding and semantics outside the VM. These tests run the same
+// macros inside the VM: installed in a Code object and flushed by
+// CPU::FlushICache, the VM-dependent ones against a real Thread, object
+// pool and heap. The order follows M3-BOOT-PLAN G2: constants first, then
+// arithmetic, memory and branches, then the Thread and heap users.
+//
+// Section numbers in comments refer to work/abi/ABI-SPEC.md.
+
+// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Assembly helpers linked into run_vm_tests (ELFv2 functions).
+//
+// ppc64_sentinel_call(fn, a0, a1, a2, a3, out): calls fn(a0..a3) with
+// r12 = fn, r14-r31 = 0x5e710000 + n * 0x101, f14-f31 = the bits
+// 0x40f00000_000000nn and CR2/CR3/CR4 = 0xa/0x5/0xc. Then it stores what the
+// callee left in r14-r31 (out[0..17]), f14-f31 (out[18..35]) and the CR
+// (out[36]), and r2 after and before the call (out[37], out[38]); restores
+// everything and returns fn's r3. The ELFv2 callee-saved contract, checked
+// from outside the code under test (stub_code_ppc64_test.cc uses it too).
+//
+// ppc64_dirty_int32_result(): returns 0xdeadbeef_80000001 in r3, an "int32"
+// result with a dirty upper word, as a foreign callee may (ABI-SPEC 7.6).
+//
+// ppc64_return_r12(): returns the r12 it was entered with.
+// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
